# cytokine — the innate first response to a held infection
#
# we model ONLY the cytokine response here; the infection itself is a fixed dose.
# pathogens is a HELD node (no flow touches it, so it sits at its level) that the
# production flow only *reads* — the same trick as french-flag's morphogen.
# it must be a node, not an external: an external read by `of` evaluates to 0,
# so production would never start.
#
# why production reads pathogens (proportional) instead of constant(c):
#   it records the causation. no infection, no response — set pathogens to 0 and
#   cytokines fall to 0. a constant would pump cytokines into a healthy body.
# why cytokines aren't made *from* pathogens:
#   cytokines are not pathogen mass, so the material comes from an external
#   `cells` source; pathogens only *set the rate*, it isn't converted.
#
# settles at steady state: cytokines = (k_make * pathogens) / k_clear = 13.3
node pathogens : range(0, 2000), init(1000)         # the dose — held, only read
node cytokines : range(0, 50),   init(0)   @ bucket
external cells                                       # immune cells secreting cytokine
external diffusion                                   # clearance / wash-out

cells     -> cytokines : proportional(of = pathogens, k = 0.004)   # production tracks load
cytokines -> diffusion : proportional(of = cytokines, k = 0.3)     # cleared faster the fuller it is

pathway pathogen_response : cells->cytokines, cytokines->diffusion
